speechtext:
I hope so. The right hon. gentleman said at the time that he would
[Mr. Lawson.}
appoint a parliamentary committee. I tell him that when that committee is appointed we shall1 be very glad-and when I say "we," I mean myse'lf and those who may have had any part in the Sage broadcasts-to go before that committee, and then it will be determined whether or not the statements made were true.
